      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 47
      },
      "description": "EXPERIMENTAL. Fitted apparent capacity at the latest used drive as % of the fitted capacity at the first used drive, at reference conditions (mean temperature), with the 95 % date-clustered bootstrap interval. It measures energy out per % SOC from drives, not a capacity test. Limits: it relies on the BMS state of charge, which on an LFP pack drifts between full charges; pack current and voltage are sampled every 30 s, so short peaks are missed; drives with less than 5 % SOC used are not used. It is an apparent capacity index, not a capacity test, and is not part of the health score. Method adapted from Packfade (https://github.com/pgodlews/packfade, MIT licence) by the same author.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
